# TLS 1.2 client: the handshake message size cap applies to the header of
# every message a client receives.
#
# The UUT is configured to accept handshake message bodies of at most 4096
# bytes (`uut.max_handshake_message_size`). Each over-limit case sends a
# message whose header announces 4097 bytes and then only the bare 4-byte
# handshake header (`pad to` grows the body to the announced size; `fragment 4
# hold_all` sends the first 4-byte record and withholds the rest), so a peer
# that enforces the cap from the header alone rejects at once, while one that
# waits for (and buffers) the announced body sends nothing and the case fails
# when no alert arrives. Each over-limit case has an at-limit control: the
# same delivery announcing exactly 4096 bytes, which must NOT be refused; the
# peer stays silent through `wait 300 ms`, waiting for the rest of the message.
# The pair pins the comparison (`length > cap`) on every message type this
# role receives. The 65536 pair repeats the first message at Botan's default
# cap, where 65537 (0x010001) needs the high byte of the 24-bit length.
#
# No RFC sets a handshake message size limit (the 24-bit length allows up to
# 2^24 - 1 bytes); the cap is local policy. Only shims whose library can apply
# one cap to every handshake message type run these cases; the others refuse
# the knob and SKIP (shims/DESIGN.md, "Corpus-enabled knob matrix").

plzn tls "client/tls12-max-handshake-message-size/server-hello-over-limit" {
  syntax 1.1
  rfc 5246 section 7.4
  chain: [ecdsa_p256]
  uut client {
    versions: [tls12]
    max_handshake_message_size: 4096
  }
  flow handshake until send ServerHello {
    send ServerHello @ pad to 4097, @ fragment 4 hold_all
  }
  expect alert fatal/handshake_failure
}

plzn tls "client/tls12-max-handshake-message-size/server-hello-at-limit" {
  syntax 1.1
  rfc 5246 section 7.4
  chain: [ecdsa_p256]
  uut client {
    versions: [tls12]
    max_handshake_message_size: 4096
  }
  flow handshake until send ServerHello {
    send ServerHello @ pad to 4096, @ fragment 4 hold_all
    wait 300 ms
  }
  expect ok
}

